<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salah Rais</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1488–1556</span> · Also known as Salih Reis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salah Rais (c. 1488–1556) was an Ottoman corsair and admiral who served as beylerbey of the Regency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> from 1552 to 1556. A veteran of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayreddin-barbarossa">Hayreddin Barbarossa</a>'s campaigns, he extended Algerian power into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> and over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a> and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Bejaia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1555. He died of plague in 1556 while preparing an attack on Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a>.</p></div>
